<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Abéché</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1909">1909</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wadai-war">Wadai War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abeche">Abéché</a> was the French capture of Abéché, capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wadai-empire">Wadai Empire</a>, in 1909. French colonial forces defeated the sultan's army and occupied the city. The battle effectively ended Wadai's independence, although resistance continued for several years.</p></div>
